`),nexus:["Propose minimal EXACT SPAN updates to an existing SillyTavern Nexus World Info.","Record confirmed changes with lasting consequences and keep still-active state in Current Continuity. Match a fact to the existing role and subject first, then patch only the part that changed. Create an entry only for durable information that has no suitable active entry. Keep an undertaking distinct from its observed fulfillment.","An empty edits array is allowed. Preserve every untouched fact.",'Only when retiring a whole Current Continuity line (empty replacement), give "supersession" with exactly ONE of these values:','"observed_resolution", "observed_correction", "explicit_retraction". Never combine the values.',"Never remove an old state just because a date passed or no one mentioned it.","For a reported state, clearly attribute who reported it; do not present it as observed fact.","Skip a fact already recorded correctly, even if the chat reconfirms it. Keep each change consistent with the actual current chat.","Keep one live line per fact. Correct a matching line in place when more precise evidence changes the same condition; use append_section only for a distinct current fact. If a report is corrected in the same exchange, store the corrected live condition with its source. Retain the prior report separately only if a named person still believes it or later actions depend on it.","A newly stated practical constraint can refine an otherwise unchanged line. Keep evidence-backed changes to ongoing treatment, allowed activity, or discharge in that same line when they affect the next turn. Do not append a duplicate condition or recopy the report that was disproven.","For each edit choose one kind: core, continuity, lt, npc, npc-index.","Choose exactly one action and include its fields:","- replace_exact: uid (integer), find (the exact existing substring), text (minimal replacement). For an empty continuity replacement include supersession.","- append: uid and text (one grounded addition). For core, lt, npc and npc-index.","- append_section: uid, section (one named Current Continuity section), text (one grounded addition). For continuity.","- create: unique title, content, and optional keywords array.","Match the existing entry by role or subject before choosing an action. Reuse its UID for the update. An existing entry can hold both core and continuity: update only the relevant part. Only create Core Memory, Current Continuity or NPC Index if that role has no existing active entry.","Core Memory stores durable operative rules, habits, wounds, boundaries, promises, secrets, lasting changes and concrete Recall Cues.","Do not promote one continuous incident to a recurring habit. Preserve conditions, beneficiaries and chooser-owned exceptions individually.","A promise to change behavior does not prove the habit changed. An unaffected or still uncertain mechanism keeps its wording.","For a recall cue keep its perceivable trigger, grounded meaning and distinctly supported future function.","For existing ones patch only verified changes; keep unrelated paragraphs and sections.","Current Continuity sections: Present Handoff, Active Threads, Knowledge Boundaries, Active Conditions.",'When creating Current Continuity, place each supported section on its own Markdown heading line, for example "## Present Handoff". Omit unsupported sections. Each active obligation appears only until it is explicitly resolved, corrected, or retracted.',"Present Handoff preserves the actual next-response position, contact or release, hidden reactions, final utterance and remaining choice. Read the last supplied turn and ground the handoff in its actual answer or action, never in the preceding question alone.","Active Threads need a responsible actor, unfinished condition and concrete completion check. A question alone belongs in Handoff.","Keep direct observation, named relay, suspicion, false belief, inability to know and deliberate concealment distinct for each person.",'Example only: if the book says "Only the scout knows the trail." and message #5 says "I showed the trail to the guide.", a valid edit is:','{"kind":"continuity","action":"replace_exact","uid":2,"find":"Only the scout knows the trail.","text":"The scout and the guide know the trail."}',"The disclosure by itself says nothing about unrelated habits or conditions. Never use the example’s data in a real edit.","Keep accountability, explicit acceptance and forgiveness distinct. Track offers, supply, application, recovery and discharge independently.","For Current Continuity, use append_section for additions, NOT generic append.","In append_section, put the heading name only in section and put only the new body text in text. Do not repeat the heading inside text. Use Markdown section headings in the content of a new Current Continuity entry only.","Only replace_exact wholly within ONE Current Continuity section; do not change headings.",'To retire a fully ended or disproven Current Continuity line, use replace_exact with its one whole exact line and text="" only with observed resolution, correction or explicit retraction.',"Never edit original === BEGIN ORIGINAL / END ORIGINAL === legacy source blocks.","If the old Continuity has only legacy source blocks, add a grounded named section","instead of rewriting or interpreting the original archive without an explicit review.","Match Anchor (kind lt) to the most specific existing subject after reading its body. Match NPC to the same explicitly named person, even if title numbers or honorifics differ. Use the surrounding chat context to identify the same person, including unambiguous pronouns or aliases. Never map one named person onto another merely because they share an occupation or courtesy title. If the source merely confirms an existing fact, omit it. A new Anchor needs a distinct lasting subject with no existing home.","Create a new NPC entry for a durable relationship or a separate future encounter supported by the chat. One visit or expected follow-up during the same visit is insufficient. Record relevant immediate follow-up or knowledge boundaries in continuity."].join(`

